{{also|bara|Bara|bára|Bára|bāra|bæra|bara-}}
==Swedish==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|sv|bʰer}}
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|bæra}}, from {{inh|sv|non|bera}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*beraną}}, from {{der|sv|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}.
Cognate with Danish {{m|da|bære}} and Norwegian {{m|no|bære}}. <ref>{{R:runeberg.org|svetym|0166.html bära}}</ref>

See the English verb {{m|en|bear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Sv-bära.ogg|audio|lang=sv}}

===Verb===
{{head|sv|verb}}

# to [[carry]]; to lift and transport anywhere else
# to [[wear]]; e.g. a piece of clothing or jewelery
# (''somewhat dated'') to [[lead]] to; end up at

